<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Idistaviso</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Idistaviso was fought in 16 CE on a plain near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser">Weser</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, between eight Roman legions with auxiliaries under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germanicus">Germanicus</a> and a coalition of Germanic tribes led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arminius">Arminius</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a> describes it as a heavy Roman victory that partly avenged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutoburg-forest">Teutoburg Forest</a> disaster of 9 CE. Arminius escaped, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> soon gave up plans to conquer Germany beyond the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-idistaviso.jpg" alt="Battle of Idistaviso" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dr. Paul Knotel (The original uploader was Sebastianwallroth at German Wikipedia.) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Idistaviso.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
